---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import PassportPhoto from '../../components/tools/PassportPhoto';
import RelatedTools from '../../components/layout/RelatedTools';
import { relatedTools } from '../../data/related-tools';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Passport Photo Maker Free Online — All Countries | Filekrush"
  description="Create passport photos for any country. Correct dimensions, white background. Runs in your browser — no upload."
  canonical="/passport-photo"
  heading="Passport Photo Maker"
  subheading="Create passport photos for any country — correct size, white background, instant."
>
  <PassportPhoto client:only="react" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <div class="toc">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#countries">Supported countries</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why-it-matters">Why exact specs matter</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 id="countries">Supported countries</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Country</th>
            <th>Photo size</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/india/">India</a></td>
            <td>51 &times; 51mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/usa/">United States</a></td>
            <td>51 &times; 51mm (2 &times; 2in)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/uk/">United Kingdom</a></td>
            <td>35 &times; 45mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/schengen/">Schengen Visa</a></td>
            <td>35 &times; 45mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/canada/">Canada</a></td>
            <td>50 &times; 70mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/australia/">Australia</a></td>
            <td>35 &times; 45mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/japan/">Japan</a></td>
            <td>35 &times; 45mm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/passport-photo/china/">China</a></td>
            <td>33 &times; 48mm</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Don't see your country? More are coming soon — in the meantime, pick the closest match above and adjust manually, or use <a href="/resize/">Resize Image</a> with your country's exact dimensions.</p>

      <h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Select your country</strong> — dimensions are set automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Drop your photo</strong> — any clear face photo works.</li>
        <li><strong>Position the crop</strong> — drag to center your face in the frame.</li>
        <li><strong>Download</strong> — your passport photo is ready at the exact required size.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="why-it-matters">Why exact specs matter</h2>
      <p>Passport and visa photos aren't just about looking presentable — printing labs and government portals check dimensions, aspect ratio, face coverage, and background color against a strict spec. A photo that's the wrong size or has a shadowed background gets your application bounced back, costing days you may not have before a deadline.</p>
      <p>If you're applying online rather than printing a physical photo, the portal usually also caps the file in KB. Once you've cropped to the right dimensions here, run the download through <a href="/compress/for-government/">Compress for Government Forms</a> if the file is too large to upload.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

      <h3>Can I use a selfie?</h3>
      <p>It's not recommended. Front-camera selfies taken up close introduce lens distortion that skews your face proportions during cropping. Use the rear camera at arm's length, or have someone else take the photo, against a plain white or light background.</p>

      <h3>Does the background need to be pure white?</h3>
      <p>For most countries, yes — a plain white or off-white background is required, with no shadows or patterns. Some countries (like the UK) allow light grey. Check your specific country page for the exact requirement.</p>

      <h3>Can I wear glasses in the photo?</h3>
      <p>Most countries now prohibit glasses in passport and visa photos, even if you normally wear them, due to glare and eye-visibility requirements. Remove glasses before photographing.</p>

      <h3>My country's portal also has a file size limit — what do I do?</h3>
      <p>Download your cropped photo here first, then run it through <a href="/compress/for-government/">Compress for Government Forms</a> to hit the exact KB range your portal specifies. Resize (dimensions) and compress (file size) are separate steps — you often need both.</p>

      <h3>Will this guarantee my application gets accepted?</h3>
      <p>This tool matches your photo to publicly documented dimension specs, but final acceptance depends on the reviewing authority. Always double check current requirements against your country's official guidance before submitting.</p>
    </section>

    <RelatedTools title="Passport photo by country" tools={relatedTools.passportPhoto} />
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
